B2 verification: printer-strings-uri merge path
================================================

Date: 2026-08-17
Testbed: same isolated CUPS instance as B1 (port 8631) + CPDB CUPS
         backend from source tree + cpdb-text-frontend.
         Harness: /tmp/cpdb-b2test.sh.
         Raw output: b2-raw-output.log (this directory).

Background / prior assumption
-----------------------------
Earlier analysis assumed the `printer-strings-uri` branch in
get_option_translation() / get_choice_translation() could NOT be
exercised through CUPS 2.4.7 for local queues.  That assumption turned
out to be WRONG: CUPS 2.4.7 cupsd DOES expose printer-strings-uri for
every queue (local and remote), pointing at a cache-hosted strings
file:

    http://<cupsd>/strings/printer-<name>.strings

The backend's request for the "printer-strings-uri" attribute succeeds,
and cupsd answers with a GET of that cache file.  The reason the path
looked untested before is that the cache file is EMPTY (0 bytes) when
the queue's PPD carries no localized strings, so cfCatalogLoad() adds
nothing and the system catalog is used - which is exactly the intended
fallback.

Verification procedure
----------------------
1. Set up the isolated CUPS testbed with three queues (printer-1,
   printer-2, printer-ipp) exactly like B1.
2. After cupsd starts, populate the cache strings file that cupsd
   serves for printer-1:
       $BASE/cache/printer-1.strings
   with printer-specific overrides in text/strings format:
       "print-color-mode"              = "Printer Color Mode"
       "print-color-mode.monochrome"   = "Printer Monochrome"
       "print-color-mode.color"        = "Printer Colour"
       "copies"                        = "Printer Copies"
       "job-sheets"                    = "Printer Job Sheets"
3. Run cpdb-text-frontend under de_DE.UTF-8 (German), so the system
   catalog would produce "Farbdruckmodus" / "Monochrom" / "Farbe" if
   the printer-strings-uri merge did NOT take place.
4. Issue, in order:
       get-option-translation print-color-mode printer-1 CUPS
       get-choice-translation print-color-mode monochrome printer-1 CUPS
       get-choice-translation print-color-mode color printer-1 CUPS

Observed results (b2-raw-output.log)
------------------------------------
    Obtained translation=Printer Color Mode;
      option=print-color-mode; locale=de_DE.UTF-8; printer=printer-1#CUPS
    Obtained translation=Printer Monochrome;
      option=print-color-mode; choice=monochrome; ...
    Obtained translation=Printer Colour;
      option=print-color-mode; choice=color; ...

i.e. the printer-specific strings file OVERRODE the German system
catalog.  cfCatalogLookUpOption() / cfCatalogLookUpChoice() consult the
printer_options catalog FIRST, which is why "Printer Color Mode" (from
printer-1.strings) wins over "Farbdruckmodus" (from cups_de.po).

cupsd access evidence (error_log):
    [Client 33x] GET /strings/printer-1.strings HTTP/1.1
    [Client 33x] Processing GET /strings/printer-1.strings
    -> the backend's cfCatalogLoad(uri, ...) fetched the file over HTTP.

Negative control: the same queue with an EMPTY strings cache file
(original state) returns the German system translations
("Farbdruckmodus" / "Monochrom"), as captured in B1 scenario 1.  This
proves the merge is driven by the printer-strings-uri content and not
by something else.

Note on printer-ipp queue
-------------------------
The B2 testbed also contains queue printer-ipp with
DeviceURI ipp://localhost:8632/ipp/print pointing at an ippeveprinter
instance serving its own /en.strings.  cupsd did NOT relay the remote
printer-strings-uri to the backend (cupsd serves its own cached
attributes for Get-Printer-Attributes), so the remote-printer case
behaves identically to the local case: the backend reads the strings
URI cupsd hands out.  This is consistent: CPDB reads translations from
the CUPS server it talks to, which for printer-strings-uri is always
cupsd's own /strings/printer-<name>.strings.

Conclusion
----------
PASS.  The printer-strings-uri merge path in get_option_translation()
and get_choice_translation() (backend_helper.c ~line 2782 / ~line 2828)
was exercised end-to-end with real CUPS 2.4.7 and verified to override
the system catalog correctly, with the documented fallback when the
strings file is empty.  No errors, no crashes; this path was part of
the B3 leak-fix scope (g_variant_builder / ippDelete / g_free fixes in
the surrounding translation code) and is now covered by an executable
verification.